WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:03.480
The church?

00:03.480 --> 00:09.360
Yes. The bandits attempted to raid this wagon
for goods connected to the church.

00:09.970 --> 00:13.860
They weren't told what exactly
 they were, however.

00:13.860 --> 00:18.870
So they attacked us without knowing 
what they should take?

00:19.340 --> 00:24.380
They intended to kill the lot of us 
and make off with all the cargo.

00:24.380 --> 00:25.620
How awful.

00:27.970 --> 00:30.000
<i>To appoint the next head,</i>

00:30.000 --> 00:33.380
<i>the nuns said they needed official 
authorization from church HQ.</i>

00:33.380 --> 00:36.090
<i>Was someone trying to prevent that?</i>

00:36.590 --> 00:41.470
<i>Maybe it's coincidence, but it feels like 
escorting this wagon was the right choice.</i>

02:14.030 --> 02:15.990
Good work, everyone!

02:16.290 --> 02:20.490
I made it safely to Bayreun thanks to you!

02:21.010 --> 02:25.370
Here are your certificates of job completion. 
Take these to the guild.

02:26.150 --> 02:29.620
I'm glad we all made it here.

02:29.620 --> 02:31.720
Yeah. That's what matters most.

02:31.720 --> 02:33.000
Absolutely!

02:33.440 --> 02:36.010
I'll hire you again if I need anything.

02:37.950 --> 02:42.260
Now that we've reported in to the guild,
 what are you two going to do next?

02:42.820 --> 02:45.700
We're headed straight to Kilmont.

02:45.700 --> 02:46.640
What about you?

02:47.140 --> 02:49.360
We're on our way to Farnid.

02:49.360 --> 02:50.390
Is that so?

02:50.880 --> 02:54.010
I'm sure we'll meet again if it's meant to be.

02:54.010 --> 02:55.940
If you see us, say hi.

02:55.940 --> 02:56.690
Sure.

02:56.690 --> 02:57.960
Take care.

02:59.780 --> 03:04.090
Well, how shall we continue 
our journey? Another wagon?

03:04.090 --> 03:06.170
Do you prefer to travel by wagon?

03:06.170 --> 03:08.810
It <i>was</i> pretty comfortable.

03:08.810 --> 03:11.170
If a bit painful on the posterior...

03:12.370 --> 03:17.250
Farnid is a pretty long way away.
Thinking ahead, it wouldn't hurt to own one.

03:18.050 --> 03:19.670
Okay, let's buy our own.

03:23.950 --> 03:26.930
They're all pretty much the same.

03:27.570 --> 03:29.890
We'll have to modify one.

03:29.890 --> 03:33.310
Hold on. Did I just hear you 
make a terrible suggestion?

03:33.970 --> 03:35.800
Whatever do you mean?

03:35.800 --> 03:37.320
You know what you said.

03:37.870 --> 03:43.180
I just want to reduce the shaking 
and improve the wheel movement.

03:43.180 --> 03:45.260
It should make it nicer to ride in.

03:45.260 --> 03:46.330
Really?

03:46.330 --> 03:49.500
It won't move without horses 
or fly through the sky?

03:49.500 --> 03:50.330
I wouldn't do that!

03:51.210 --> 03:53.510
In other words, you <i>could</i>.

03:55.430 --> 03:58.010
Well, as long as it isn't too flashy...

03:58.010 --> 04:01.470
That's the idea.
I'm still feeling all this out, you know.

04:01.800 --> 04:04.580
I'd believe that coming from anyone else.

04:04.580 --> 04:06.970
Aren't you being mean to me
for no reason?

04:07.630 --> 04:09.720
So, which one should we get?

04:09.720 --> 04:13.850
I'd like one large enough to sleep in.

04:14.700 --> 04:15.850
So...

04:16.620 --> 04:17.860
about that size?

04:17.860 --> 04:19.360
You're right.

04:19.360 --> 04:23.400
There's room for luggage, and we'll be 
all set for when my master arrives.

04:23.400 --> 04:24.330
You're right.

04:24.930 --> 04:27.370
Excuse me! I'd like to buy this.

04:28.570 --> 04:31.120
We'll pick it up on our way out of town.

04:31.120 --> 04:32.130
Sure thing!

04:32.130 --> 04:35.370
By the way, have you already acquired horses?

04:35.370 --> 04:37.410
No, not yet.

04:37.410 --> 04:39.130
Then I've got a little advice for you.

04:39.500 --> 04:43.520
You'll want to get horses 
with good legs to pull this wagon.

04:43.520 --> 04:47.010
It's a bit too heavy for one horse, too.

04:47.330 --> 04:51.570
I've heard rumors about people 
using monsters to pull their wagons.

04:51.570 --> 04:55.020
Some do. After all, they're way stronger.

04:55.450 --> 04:58.260
You have to be able to tame one, though.

04:58.260 --> 05:01.030
I see. Thanks. I'll take that 
into consideration.

05:03.810 --> 05:07.180
We can have Yuzuha transform 
if we get desperate.

05:09.990 --> 05:11.540
That's a telepathic call alert.

05:12.150 --> 05:14.290
<i>This is Shin. Is that you, Schnee?</i>

05:14.290 --> 05:17.980
<i>Yes. I've concluded my business 
in the kingdom.</i>

05:17.980 --> 05:19.170
<i>Where are you now?</i>

05:19.860 --> 05:22.670
<i>We just bought a wagon in Bayreun.</i>

05:23.190 --> 05:26.640
<i>After this, we need to find horses
to set out for Farnid.</i>

05:26.640 --> 05:30.630
<i>In that case, allow me to capture 
a monster to pull the wagon.</i>

05:32.500 --> 05:36.090
<i>I'll arrive in Bayreun within a day.</i>

05:36.090 --> 05:38.780
<i>Could you wait for me there?</i>

05:38.780 --> 05:41.820
<i>Sure. You don't need to rush.</i>

05:42.140 --> 05:46.070
<i>Thank you. Also, regarding the Moon Sanctum...</i>

05:46.660 --> 05:50.700
<i>The castle was quite concerned
over its sudden disappearance.</i>

05:50.980 --> 05:54.700
<i>Seriously? They're that worried 
just because I packed it up?</i>

05:55.060 --> 05:57.400
<i>Everyone was rather pale.</i>

05:57.400 --> 05:59.640
<i>This will do them good, though.</i>

05:59.640 --> 06:00.830
<i>How so?</i>

06:00.830 --> 06:07.040
<i>Honestly, I was getting fed up
with their incessant flattery</i>

06:07.040 --> 06:09.500
<i>while trying to observe and recruit me.</i>

06:09.500 --> 06:12.220
<i>Ah, yeah. That must be rough.</i>

06:12.630 --> 06:14.860
<i>I'm sure any kingdom looking</i>

06:14.860 --> 06:18.380
<i>to bolster its military 
would want you in their ranks.</i>

06:18.380 --> 06:22.730
<i>Yes. One kingdom even dared to claim 
ownership of the Moon Sanctum.</i>

06:23.710 --> 06:26.990
<i>I considered eradicating the entire nation.</i>

06:26.990 --> 06:30.010
<i>That's no joke coming from you.</i>

06:30.010 --> 06:33.870
<i>Maybe they thought they'd get you 
if they acquired the Moon Sanctum.</i>

06:34.290 --> 06:36.580
<i>Indeed, there have been people who tried.</i>

06:36.580 --> 06:38.840
<i>And also those who proposed marriage.</i>

06:38.840 --> 06:39.870
<i>Yeah, I bet.</i>

06:40.260 --> 06:45.280
<i>I'm the one who made her that way, 
but Schnee is a total knockout.</i>

06:45.280 --> 06:46.940
<i>It's no wonder she's popular.</i>

06:46.940 --> 06:48.380
<i>Are you jealous?</i>

06:49.590 --> 06:51.030
<i>Well, yeah.</i>

06:53.580 --> 06:56.770
<i>I see. You're jealous over me.</i>

06:57.730 --> 06:59.300
<i>Where did that come from?</i>

06:59.300 --> 07:00.690
<i>Figure it out.</i>

07:03.140 --> 07:06.330
<i>Now then, let me know
once you've found an inn.</i>

07:06.330 --> 07:09.260
<i>Sure, you got it. Talk to you then.</i>

07:13.140 --> 07:14.450
Aren't these pretty?

07:14.450 --> 07:19.130
Yeah. It might be nice to wander and 
take in the sights while we look for an inn.

07:19.130 --> 07:21.540
Are you from out of town?

07:21.540 --> 07:25.130
If you haven't found an inn yet, 
I can tell you where's good!

07:28.050 --> 07:29.560
This seems...

07:29.560 --> 07:31.410
Expensive.

07:33.300 --> 07:34.570
Welcome.

07:35.700 --> 07:37.920
We're looking for a place to stay.

07:37.920 --> 07:40.050
Will you be sharing a room?

07:41.100 --> 07:42.660
S-Separate rooms, please!

07:42.660 --> 07:43.810
Very well.

07:45.220 --> 07:46.440
<i>That was close.</i>

07:47.250 --> 07:51.820
I can't believe we spent 
almost half our reward on an inn.

07:52.170 --> 07:55.820
That woman recommended 
one heck of a place to stay.

07:56.170 --> 07:59.880
Maybe she thought adventurers could afford it.

07:59.880 --> 08:04.080
It's apparently famous in Bayreun, 
and it's not bad to indulge once in a while.

08:06.840 --> 08:08.930
It's definitely a luxury inn.

08:14.670 --> 08:16.090
Can I talk now?

08:16.500 --> 08:19.040
Yeah. It should be fine here.

08:19.040 --> 08:20.850
It's so fluffy!

08:21.740 --> 08:24.560
Rolly, rolly! Rolly, rolly! Ack!

08:22.430 --> 08:24.560
We have some time until dinner.

08:24.560 --> 08:26.860
Guess I'll do maintenance on my weapons.

08:31.190 --> 08:33.160
Shin, do you have a minute?

08:33.160 --> 08:34.780
Sure. The door's open.

08:36.420 --> 08:40.250
Did you tell my master 
we're staying in this city?

08:40.250 --> 08:40.870
Yeah.

08:41.390 --> 08:45.170
I don't know exactly when, but she 
said she'd arrive in Bayreun tomorrow.

08:45.170 --> 08:48.480
I see. Then we should get some rest.

08:48.480 --> 08:51.570
Yeah. Let's have dinner in the room.

08:55.380 --> 08:56.800
I'm stuffed.

08:56.800 --> 08:59.710
I'll take a quick bath,
then go straight to bed.

09:01.330 --> 09:04.020
You'll turn into a fox for the night, right?

09:06.230 --> 09:09.400
Perhaps I'll take a bath and go to bed, too.

09:09.810 --> 09:12.120
I wanna take a bath together!

09:12.120 --> 09:13.360
Sure. That's fine.

09:13.360 --> 09:15.280
Yay! Bath time!

09:17.520 --> 09:20.280
Bath, bath, bath!

09:20.790 --> 09:25.030
Wait, Yuzuha! We should use the bath in my room...

09:29.610 --> 09:32.750
Guess I'll keep working on my weapons.

09:31.730 --> 09:35.050
Wow, Tiera! Amazing!

09:35.550 --> 09:37.360
Hey, stop!

09:37.360 --> 09:38.490
They're so soft!

09:38.490 --> 09:40.050
Yuzuha, please!

09:40.050 --> 09:42.060
<i>Hey! I'm right here, you know!</i>

09:42.420 --> 09:45.620
Yuzuha, let go!

09:45.620 --> 09:47.170
Boing, boing!

09:47.630 --> 09:49.060
Don't do that!

09:53.170 --> 09:54.990
The moon's lovely tonight...

09:55.300 --> 09:59.800
Hey, Yuzuha! Come on!

10:08.870 --> 10:10.500
Not bad.

10:24.230 --> 10:26.640
<i>No wonder I can't breathe.</i>

10:28.180 --> 10:31.150
I'm going to work on the wagon 
until Schnee gets here.

10:31.590 --> 10:32.970
What are you going to do?

10:32.970 --> 10:36.560
I'm curious to see what modifications 
you'll make, so maybe I'll watch.

10:36.560 --> 10:37.650
Me too!

10:41.580 --> 10:44.660
I should probably start by altering the axles.

10:44.660 --> 10:51.440
If I do this and add some springs, 
that should reduce the shaking.

10:51.440 --> 10:53.170
Huh? What?

10:53.570 --> 10:55.170
Okay, that should do it.

10:57.100 --> 10:59.530
Now I just need to add the bearings.

11:00.210 --> 11:02.400
What was that, Shin?

11:02.400 --> 11:04.600
The metal went all bendy!

11:04.600 --> 11:07.540
It's a creation skill for working metal.

11:07.540 --> 11:09.710
Though I've adapted it a bit for this.

11:10.310 --> 11:11.440
That was fast...

11:11.440 --> 11:12.070
Huh?

11:12.940 --> 11:16.220
That was way too fast!
It hasn't even been a minute!

11:16.220 --> 11:18.770
Do modifications always take so little time?

11:20.460 --> 11:22.450
Oh, right, we're avoiding attention.

11:22.720 --> 11:26.050
I'll install the bearings 
in a more conventional fashion.

11:26.890 --> 11:27.760
Huh?

11:27.760 --> 11:28.700
<i>It's Schnee.</i>

11:29.170 --> 11:33.080
<i>I've arrived. I'm in the woods 
beyond the north gate.</i>

11:33.850 --> 11:36.180
<i>Got it. We'll head there now.</i>

11:36.180 --> 11:37.320
What is it?

11:37.320 --> 11:42.210
Schnee's here. Let's finish this up 
and meet her as fast as we can.

11:43.090 --> 11:46.250
Didn't you just say you'd do the rest normally?

11:52.770 --> 11:53.860
Something's up ahead.

11:53.860 --> 11:54.960
Yeah.

11:54.960 --> 11:55.980
What is it?

11:56.360 --> 11:59.990
Oh, um... you'll see once we get there.

12:01.670 --> 12:02.950
We're close.

12:02.950 --> 12:04.990
Shin, it's strong.

12:13.990 --> 12:16.060
Huh? What is this?

12:17.040 --> 12:23.510
<b>Monster</b>

12:17.040 --> 12:23.510
<b>Gruefazio Jade</b>

12:17.260 --> 12:19.290
A Gruefazio Jade.

12:19.710 --> 12:23.510
It's a monster whose max level 
is normally 650.

12:23.990 --> 12:29.300
But since you don't usually see them with 
horns like that, I'm guessing this one's unique.

12:29.300 --> 12:31.020
I have returned.

12:31.020 --> 12:35.730
As promised, I've brought you 
a monster to pull the wagon.

12:36.230 --> 12:40.340
This should be able to do the job
without issue.

12:40.740 --> 12:44.530
Out of curiosity, where did you get it?

12:44.900 --> 12:47.580
From the nearby sacred mountain.

12:47.580 --> 12:50.460
Always going above and beyond, Schnee...

12:50.460 --> 12:52.290
You honor me.

12:52.290 --> 12:55.260
I mean, it wasn't really a compliment.

12:55.260 --> 12:59.690
She loses all reason when it comes to you.

13:06.500 --> 13:08.180
It's already taken a liking to you.

13:08.670 --> 13:12.200
They're popular with kids, 
so maybe it's the friendly type.

13:12.200 --> 13:14.560
This isn't just my problem, you know...

13:14.930 --> 13:18.200
Well, now that we've brought it here, 
we're stuck with it.

13:18.200 --> 13:20.080
Why did you choose this monster?

13:20.080 --> 13:22.570
If it is to pull your wagon,

13:23.020 --> 13:26.800
I knew it had to be a monster
in the sacred beast class.

13:26.800 --> 13:30.040
Come on, now! It's way too big.

13:30.040 --> 13:32.420
What kind of wagon were you 
expecting me to get?

13:32.420 --> 13:35.620
I anticipated you would say that, Shin.

13:35.620 --> 13:36.530
What?

13:38.900 --> 13:40.590
Go on. Do it.

13:52.680 --> 13:54.180
It shrank?

13:54.660 --> 13:56.980
So it has that ability, huh?

13:57.530 --> 14:00.260
It can go even smaller.

14:00.260 --> 14:02.480
It will be quite convenient 
for staying at inns.

14:02.840 --> 14:05.870
You're right. This size should be fine.

14:06.870 --> 14:08.510
I'm strangely exhausted...

14:09.670 --> 14:13.990
It was intimidating enough before
to make most people faint.

14:13.990 --> 14:15.430
Yeah, you're right.

14:15.910 --> 14:19.880
You're both crazy for carrying on
like it was no big deal.

14:19.880 --> 14:24.750
Still, I never expected her 
to bring something so high-level.

14:25.040 --> 14:27.280
Did I do something wrong?

14:27.280 --> 14:32.420
Master! Most people wouldn't even think
of making a sacred beast pull a wagon.

14:32.930 --> 14:35.340
Do you not like it?

14:35.340 --> 14:36.020
What?

14:38.120 --> 14:40.540
Wait, wait! Why are you getting sad?

14:40.540 --> 14:42.060
I don't have a problem with it.

14:42.060 --> 14:45.670
I'm happy to have a cool 
sacred beast pull my wagon.

14:54.210 --> 14:57.160
He says, "You can count on me."

14:57.980 --> 15:00.340
You two monsters 
can communicate with each other?

15:00.340 --> 15:02.310
He really is a sacred beast!

15:07.320 --> 15:10.010
By the way, what's his name?

15:10.010 --> 15:11.660
His name is Shimmer.

15:11.660 --> 15:15.260
He can use illusion and thunder skills.

15:15.260 --> 15:18.870
Shimmer, huh? Nice to meet you.

15:19.780 --> 15:22.570
Mind your manners around my master.

15:25.860 --> 15:29.070
Okay, Shimmer. Our first destination is Farnid.

15:29.770 --> 15:34.160
We're going to see an old friend named Girart.

15:34.560 --> 15:37.550
So let's go! Take us to him!

15:42.310 --> 15:44.540
This is great! It feels amazing!

15:50.780 --> 15:54.430
I guess we're still drawing attention, 
despite my best efforts.

15:54.770 --> 15:57.490
Well, there's nothing we can do about that.

15:57.490 --> 15:58.920
It really is incredible, though.

15:58.920 --> 16:01.810
The wagon doesn't shake at all, 
and my rear doesn't hurt.

16:02.340 --> 16:05.410
It outperforms even a royal carriage.

16:05.410 --> 16:09.940
I've ridden in one before, 
and it wasn't this comfortable.

16:17.300 --> 16:19.010
What are you talking about?

16:19.010 --> 16:20.950
Shimmer's childhood.

16:21.430 --> 16:25.460
Shimmer and his mom used to rule 
the sacred mountain together.

16:25.890 --> 16:30.630
But an adventurer defeated his mom, 
and only Shimmer survived.

16:31.100 --> 16:33.100
An adventurer, huh?

16:34.070 --> 16:38.470
<i>I'm ashamed to admit 
I did similar things in the game.</i>

16:38.470 --> 16:42.980
He ran as fast as he could 
and was rescued by an elf girl.

16:43.900 --> 16:48.060
Then he worked hard to get stronger 
and return to the sacred mountain.

16:48.580 --> 16:50.590
An elf, was it?

16:50.590 --> 16:53.990
No wonder he wasn't 
especially cautious around me.

16:58.070 --> 17:02.010
He says he followed you 
because you smelled familiar.

17:02.410 --> 17:03.990
Familiar?

17:05.000 --> 17:07.380
He says it was Tiera's smell.

17:07.940 --> 17:09.000
Me?

17:09.000 --> 17:13.010
Was Tiera the elf girl who rescued you?

17:14.340 --> 17:15.540
Yeah!

17:15.540 --> 17:16.510
Seriously?!

17:18.060 --> 17:19.260
Come to think of it,

17:20.050 --> 17:24.170
I did save an injured puppy when I was a child.

17:24.170 --> 17:27.600
I thought they looked similar, but...

17:27.920 --> 17:29.290
Could it really be?

17:31.010 --> 17:33.040
He says you met over a century ago.

17:33.040 --> 17:37.360
Then it is him! I see... So you're that puppy.

17:39.120 --> 17:43.520
Then why don't I transfer ownership
of Shimmer to you, Tiera?

17:43.520 --> 17:44.500
What?

17:44.500 --> 17:46.860
Will that be okay at her level?

17:47.330 --> 17:50.130
There should be no problem 
if both parties accept.

17:50.620 --> 17:54.790
I shall dissolve our contract 
and have you form a new one with Tiera.

17:58.940 --> 18:02.260
First, to dissolve the contract...

18:06.150 --> 18:08.770
May there be light where you walk.

18:18.730 --> 18:20.780
Okay, Tiera, you're next.

18:21.420 --> 18:22.220
Right!

18:34.500 --> 18:36.420
It's okay. I can do it.

18:41.960 --> 18:45.340
It is my desire to walk with you.

19:03.950 --> 19:04.580
Whoa, there.

19:05.500 --> 19:06.580
Are you okay?

19:07.730 --> 19:10.810
Sorry. I suddenly felt weak.

19:13.330 --> 19:16.260
I'm fine. I just need to rest a little.

19:23.470 --> 19:24.350
Hey, Schnee.

19:24.790 --> 19:29.080
Did you let Tiera have Shimmer 
so he could protect her?

19:29.080 --> 19:30.350
Yes, precisely.

19:30.870 --> 19:34.010
We can't always be by her side,

19:34.580 --> 19:40.880
and I'd feel better knowing Shimmer is 
with her when she chooses her own path.

19:40.880 --> 19:44.970
Now that they've formed an ownership 
contract, she can summon Shimmer anytime.

19:44.970 --> 19:45.870
We can count on him.

19:46.250 --> 19:50.300
I'd come running anytime you're in trouble.

19:51.900 --> 19:52.500
Thanks.

19:54.340 --> 19:57.500
Honestly, you're the one I turn 
to when I'm really screwed.

19:58.410 --> 19:59.510
I appreciate it.

20:04.330 --> 20:05.480
Schnee?

20:05.480 --> 20:06.820
You can count on me.

20:06.820 --> 20:07.400
What?

20:08.450 --> 20:09.770
You can count on me!

20:10.780 --> 20:11.640
Thanks.

20:17.430 --> 20:19.530
This forest goes on forever.

20:20.050 --> 20:22.880
We're in southeastern Farnid.

20:22.880 --> 20:25.910
It's right on the edge of Raluah Forest.

20:29.140 --> 20:30.040
Someone's coming.

20:30.820 --> 20:32.520
They're pretty high-level.

20:32.520 --> 20:36.330
I just sent a message to Girart.
They must be here to meet us.

20:41.310 --> 20:43.050
I thought you might come.

20:48.130 --> 20:50.730
We came on orders of the First King.

20:50.730 --> 20:51.860
Are they the ones?

20:52.650 --> 20:55.940
Yes. Please take us to Girart.

20:56.530 --> 20:59.440
Very well. We'll show you to the mansion.

21:13.260 --> 21:15.590
Hey, do you know those two?

21:15.590 --> 21:18.420
They're Girart's grandchildren.

21:18.420 --> 21:19.210
Seriously?

21:36.500 --> 21:39.180
We've brought Schnee's party.

21:39.180 --> 21:40.470
Enter.

21:59.450 --> 22:03.980
Hey, Master. I didn't think I'd get 
to see you again in this life.

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time
Episode 8
<b>Trusted and Entrusted</b></b>
